Z||000005||286SE'S||07-13-2000||02:16 PM||||Put me down as very interested, I have given up on ever hearing from Daytona dashboards. By natural and synthetic I guess you mean real wood veneer. Would the real wood have problems with fading from sun exposure? How would you cover the Fiero glovebox? And why?<BR>That item may not be popular. I do want the gauge surrounds, radio bezel and center shift plate. I like the look of the power window/mirror plate covered in woodgrain too.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bill Osmer||07-13-2000||03:02 PM||||I have purchased the 2 piece power door trim (which anyone can purchase from AutoDash.com)- I think the quality is excellent. However, there were no installation instructions, so it was a good thing I had done some from Dennis LaGrua before. I have received LOTS of complements RE: the wood interior I have in my Fiero - <P>IMHO<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||4
