Z||000008||Pattyb||07-14-2000||01:53 AM||||The natural wood kits are made out of a real wood veneer, backed by ten mil paper.  Both sides are coated with epoxy and put on a press to cure.  Multiple finish coats are then applied and a special ultra-violet light  protector is also included.  I have inquired about the fade stats on the natural woods and am awaiting an answer.  <P>The real carbon is woven from Carbon, Aramid, and Hybon fabrics.  They are available in a number of colors.<P>The synthetic woods and carbon fiber are an embossed foil print with UV stabilizers for non-fade.  The finish is made of a highly elasticized resin which can withstand extreme  heat and cold.  With the UV stabilizers there is a less than 2% fade over a period of 10 years.<P>Here is the layout of all the pieces.  The ones in the dashed lines are the pieces available outside of the basic kit.  Glovebox  piece is if you have a glovebox.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/jbrooke269/basekit.gif">    <P>Here are the real carbon fibers:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/jbrooke269/carbon.gif">   <P>These are the real woods. Note that the walnut burl will be an extra 5%, Red Walnut 7%, and carp. burl 10%:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/jbrooke269/realwood.gif">  <P>These are the synthetic woods and synthetic carbon fiber:<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/jbrooke269/synwood.gif">   <BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/jbrooke269/syncarb.gif"> <P> I will have a much better website up soon with everything.  If you have any questions please ask.<P>Pat<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Pattyb (edited 07-14-2000).]||||reg||1
